    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Chronic cough with daily yellow sputum, occasional streaks of blood, and breathlessness on stairs, worse in winter, for several years after an illness with blood in the sputum about eight years ago; tuberculosis, nontuberculous mycobacteria and bronchiectasis to be distinguished</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R05.3</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting concern at the index visit, superseded by the diagnosis at the consultation; it echoes her documented chest illness (D).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Non-cystic fibrosis bronchiectasis of the left lower lobe and lingula with chronic Haemophilus influenzae infection and mild airflow obstruction (Bronchiectasis Severity Index 3, mild); tuberculosis and nontuberculous mycobacterial disease excluded; synthetic modern diagnosis chosen for a historical chest illness whose cause is disputed</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>J47.9</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis; the nature of her historical chest illness remains undetermined (R, disputed).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
