    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Tdap, PCV20 and the first hepatitis B dose given today; hepatitis B and C screening sent; cervical HPV test collected. HIV was tested at her first visit. [S]<list><item>First screening mammogram at 40, next year.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Long-term opioid therapy (Z79.891)</content>. Benefits and harms reviewed: no sedation, constipation controlled, naloxone at home, the prescription monitoring program shows one prescriber and one pharmacy. She wants to stay at 8 mg twice daily over the summer before the next step. [S]<list><item>Continue morphine solution 4 mL twice daily.</item><item>Senna at night if stools go more than three days.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Prolonged grief disorder: safety review (F43.81)</content>. No thoughts of death or self-harm; the safety plan is current. [S]<list><item>Final grief session this week, with a booster session in two months.</item><item>988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline on her safety plan.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>106/66 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1; already in treatment for grief with PHQ-9 at each chronic-care visit</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never uses tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; feels safe at home</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and statin assessment</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Statin assessment begins at 40; no risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Underweight, with a normal glucose at her first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Due</td><td>Biennial mammography from 40, next year</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No record of earlier screening; high-risk HPV test collected today; repeat every five years if negative</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Begins at 45</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Negative at her first visit, as part of the tuberculosis work-up</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Once for adults 18 to 79; sent today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Once for all adults (surface antigen, surface antibody and core antibody); sent today before the first vaccine dose</td></tr><tr><td>Osteoporosis screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>DXA three months ago: Z-scores within the expected range; vitamin D repleted</td></tr><tr><td>Folic acid</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not sexually active and not planning pregnancy; she will start folic acid and review her medicines before any pregnancy</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap; no record of a booster within ten years</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 for chronic lung disease; series complete</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No record of vaccination; dose 1 of 2 today, dose 2 at the autumn review</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>At the autumn review; yearly for her lung disease</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Discuss in the autumn with the influenza vaccine</td></tr><tr><td>Human papillomavirus vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Routine vaccination ends at 26; shared decision-making to 45: not sexually active, and she chose not to have it</td></tr><tr><td>Naloxone and opioid safety</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two naloxone devices at home and in date; morphine in a locked box</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tetanus, diphtheria, and acellular pertussis vaccine (Tdap); Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine, 20-valent (PCV20); Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CDC Clinical Practice Guideline for Prescribing Opioids for Pain, United States, 2022 (2022); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Seven-month review in the autumn with the PHQ-9, sputum culture, the second hepatitis B dose and the influenza vaccine. Hepatitis B, hepatitis C and HPV results by phone. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1845-10-19: seven-month review after an exacerbation: lungs, opioid therapy, mood, safety, weight, and vaccines. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
